<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norodom Suramarit</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896–1960</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Norodom Suramarit was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> from 1955 to 1960. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a> abdicated in his favour in 1955 to enter politics and lead the Sangkum movement, so Suramarit reigned while Sihanouk governed. After his death in 1960 no king was crowned; Sihanouk became head of state, and the queen mother represented the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/norodom-suramarit.jpg" alt="Norodom Suramarit" width="320" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HeroZeWiki07 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Roi_Du_Cambodge_Sur_Le_Tr%C3%B4ne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
